{
  "_comment": "State machine of src/status_listener.js. SCENARIO groups (first_poll, armed_codes, sensor_codes, transitions, zone_indexing, failures): { name, zones, polls, expected_events, known_bug?, note? }. zones are the [enabled, name] tuples handed to statusListener() (already filtered by login(); the listener only uses their count and order). polls has one entry per 1000 ms tick: { statuszone, useraccess } makes the panel serve those tables (status code per zone; area state codes, first entry is area 1; tables have 0 or >= 2 entries because a one-entry table is a JavaScript new Array(n)); { page: { file } } serves that captured page (relative to tests/); { fail } makes the panel misbehave for this tick only: { status: n, body? } HTTP answer with that status (default body: a short error text), { connection: \"refused\" | \"reset\" } transport failure, { page: { file } } HTTP 200 with a page that has no status tables. expected_events lists, in emission order over the whole run: [\"armedChanged\", true | false | null], [\"sensorChanged\", \"<zone index as a decimal string>\", true | false], [\"error\"]. Before the first poll the listener assumes armed = null and every sensor = false; it never announces that state, only differences from it. CADENCE group (status_poll_cadence): { name, advance_ms: [...], expected_requests: [...] } advance a fake clock step by step from the creation of the listener and give the cumulative number of requests the panel has seen after each step (GET /statuslive.html). Rows with a known_bug (catalog in README.md) are in known_bugs/status_machine.json, in the same groups; zone_indexing exists only there.",
  "first_poll": [
    {
      "name": "armed panel",
      "zones": [[1, "A"], [1, "B"]],
      "polls": [{ "statuszone": [0, 0], "useraccess": [2, 0] }],
      "expected_events": [["armedChanged", true]]
    },
    {
      "name": "arming (code 7) counts as armed",
      "zones": [[1, "A"], [1, "B"]],
      "polls": [{ "statuszone": [0, 0], "useraccess": [7, 0] }],
      "expected_events": [["armedChanged", true]]
    },
    {
      "name": "open zone on the first poll: armed first, then the sensor",
      "zones": [[1, "A"], [1, "B"]],
      "polls": [{ "statuszone": [1, 0], "useraccess": [1, 0] }],
      "expected_events": [["armedChanged", false], ["sensorChanged", "0", true]]
    },
    {
      "name": "every zone open on the first poll: sensors in index order",
      "zones": [[1, "A"], [1, "B"], [1, "C"]],
      "polls": [{ "statuszone": [1, 1, 1], "useraccess": [0, 0] }],
      "expected_events": [["sensorChanged", "0", true], ["sensorChanged", "1", true], ["sensorChanged", "2", true]]
    },
    {
      "name": "only the open zone is announced on the first poll",
      "zones": [[1, "A"], [1, "B"], [1, "C"]],
      "polls": [{ "statuszone": [0, 1, 0], "useraccess": [0, 0] }],
      "expected_events": [["sensorChanged", "1", true]]
    }
  ],
